.TH YTNEF 1 "" "ytnef-rust" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytnef \- extract attachments from TNEF (winmail.dat) streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytnef
.RI [ options ] " file" ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ytnef
decodes Microsoft TNEF streams, the
.I application/ms-tnef
attachments usually named
.I winmail.dat
that Outlook sends. It can list the contents of a stream and save the
attachments it contains, converting contacts and calendar entries to vCard
and vCalendar files.
.PP
This is the Rust port of ytnef. Its flags, output and exit status match the
C tool except where the C tool was unsafe; see
.BR DIFFERENCES .
.PP
Options are read in order, so each one affects only the files named after it.
A leading
.B \-
enables an option and a leading
.B +
disables it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " +v
Enable or disable verbose output. Repeat
.B \-v
for more detail.
.TP
.BI \-f " dir"
Save attachments to
.IR dir .
.B +f
disables saving.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " +F
Enable or disable saving the message body as an RTF file.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " +H
Enable or disable saving the message body as an HTML file.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " +a
Enable or disable saving intermediate files.
.TP
.BI \-s " n"
Set the largest attachment size to accept, in megabytes (default 50).
.TP
.B \-h
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every file parsed and every output file was written; non-zero
otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ytnef \-v winmail.dat
List the contents of the stream without saving anything.
.TP
.B ytnef \-f . winmail.dat
Save all attachments to the current directory.
.TP
.B ytnef \-F \-f . winmail.dat
Also save the message text as an RTF file.
.SH DIFFERENCES
Compared with C ytnef 2.1.x:
.IP \(bu 2
Output names are a single path component. As in C,
.BR / ,
.B \e
and space become
.BR _ ;
control bytes also become
.BR _ ,
leading dots are removed and names are cut to 255 bytes.
.IP \(bu 2
Existing files and symlinks are never overwritten or followed. On a name
clash a counter goes before the extension
.RB ( x.dat " becomes " x1.dat ).
.IP \(bu 2
Embedded TNEF streams nest at most 8 deep (C: 16). An embedded stream that
fails to parse is saved as a plain attachment.
.IP \(bu 2
A failure to write a vCard, vTask or vCalendar file goes to standard error
and makes the exit status non-zero.
.IP \(bu 2
Repeating
.B \-v
does not reproduce the C library's internal parser trace.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ytnefprint (1),
.BR ytnefprocess (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef-rust
